<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 27: </span>
<span id="A5.F27.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Cost-aware tool use on the Invivo Task with implicit budget notification.</span>
<span id="A5.F27.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Left:</span> Utility gain over the no-tool baseline under varying cost constraints. Solid lines show oracle allocation (optimal top-<math id="A5.F27.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>), dashed lines show model performance with cost information, squares denote no cost-awareness, and dotted lines indicate always-calling.
<span id="A5.F27.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Right:</span> Actual tool calls without budget enforcement. Models do not reliably reduce or stop calls as cost increases, despite being provided with cost and remaining budget.
</figcaption>
</figure>
