</figure>
</section>
<section id="A5.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">E.3 </span>Controller Framework</h3>

<div id="A5.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Here, we present the confusion matrices of <math id="A5.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="LNE" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">LNE</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A5.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="LUE_{x}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>U</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>x</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">LUE_{x}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A5.SS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="LUE_{x,d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>U</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">LUE_{x,d}</annotation></semantics></math> as additional results for the InvivoQuery Task. For the <math id="A5.SS3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="LNE" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">LNE</annotation></semantics></math> in Figure <a href="#A5.F31" title="Figure 31 ‣ E.3 Controller Framework ‣ Appendix E InvivoQuery Task ‣ To Call or Not to Call:A Framework to Assess and Optimize LLM Tool Calling" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">31</span></a> and Figure <a href="#A5.F32" title="Figure 32 ‣ E.3 Controller Framework ‣ Appendix E InvivoQuery Task ‣ To Call or Not to Call:A Framework to Assess and Optimize LLM Tool Calling" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">32</span></a>. The results show that when the predictor decides to call the tool, the model indeed requires external assistance in the majority of cases (¿75%) across all models.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A5.F31" class="ltx_figure"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2605.00737v1/invivo_barplot_need_accuracy.svg" id="A5.F31.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" width="274" height="152"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 31: </span>
<span id="A5.F31.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">InvivoQuery task: The LNE can predict the <span id="A5.F31.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">True Need</span> more accurately across most models, especially for small and weaker models.</span>
</figcaption>
</figure>
