<figure id="A5.F32.sf5" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2605.00737v1/predictor_invivo_predictor1_Mistral3.1-24B_layer0_MLP_cm.svg" id="A5.F32.sf5.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_square" width="548" height="457"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">(e) </span>Mistral-3.1-24B-IT</figcaption>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_many">
<figure id="A5.F32.sf6" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2605.00737v1/predictor_invivo_predictor1_Llama3.2-3B_layer26_MLP_cm.svg" id="A5.F32.sf6.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_square" width="548" height="457"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">(f) </span>Llama-3.2-3B-IT</figcaption>
</figure></div></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 32: </span>[InvivoQuery Task.] Confusion matrix for the <math id="A5.F32.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="LNE" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">LNE</annotation></semantics></math> estimator</figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="A5.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">For <math id="A5.SS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="LUE_{x}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>U</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>x</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">LUE_{x}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A5.SS3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="LUE_{x,d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>U</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">LUE_{x,d}</annotation></semantics></math> (Figures <a href="#A5.F33" title="Figure 33 ‣ E.3 Controller Framework ‣ Appendix E InvivoQuery Task ‣ To Call or Not to Call:A Framework to Assess and Optimize LLM Tool Calling" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">33</span></a>, <a href="#A5.F34" title="Figure 34 ‣ E.3 Controller Framework ‣ Appendix E InvivoQuery Task ‣ To Call or Not to Call:A Framework to Assess and Optimize LLM Tool Calling" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">34</span></a>, and <a href="#A5.F35" title="Figure 35 ‣ E.3 Controller Framework ‣ Appendix E InvivoQuery Task ‣ To Call or Not to Call:A Framework to Assess and Optimize LLM Tool Calling" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">35</span></a>), the results show that when the predictor decides to call the tool, it yields positive utility in the majority of cases (¿50%) across all models.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A5.F33" class="ltx_figure"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2605.00737v1/predictor_invivo_invivo_barplot_pred2_vs_pred3_accuracy.svg" id="A5.F33.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" width="274" height="138"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 33: </span>
<span id="A5.F33.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">The LUE can predict the <span id="A5.F33.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">True Utility</span> more accurately across most models, especially for small and weaker models.</span>
</figcaption>
</figure>
