<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 47: </span>[BFCL Task.] Confusion matrix for the <math id="A6.F47.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="LNE" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">LNE</annotation></semantics></math> estimator</figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="A6.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">For <math id="A6.SS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="LUE_{x}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>U</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>x</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">LUE_{x}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A6.SS3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="LUE_{x,d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>U</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">LUE_{x,d}</annotation></semantics></math> (Figures <a href="#A6.F48" title="Figure 48 ‣ F.3 Controller Framework ‣ Appendix F Results for BFCL task ‣ To Call or Not to Call:A Framework to Assess and Optimize LLM Tool Calling" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">48</span></a>, <a href="#A6.F49" title="Figure 49 ‣ F.3 Controller Framework ‣ Appendix F Results for BFCL task ‣ To Call or Not to Call:A Framework to Assess and Optimize LLM Tool Calling" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">49</span></a>, and <a href="#A6.F50" title="Figure 50 ‣ F.3 Controller Framework ‣ Appendix F Results for BFCL task ‣ To Call or Not to Call:A Framework to Assess and Optimize LLM Tool Calling" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">50</span></a>), the results show that when the predictor decides to call the tool, it yields positive utility in the majority of cases (¿60%) across all models. Conversely, when the predictor decides not to call the tool, the utility is negative or neutral in most cases (¿50%).</p>
</div>
<figure id="A6.F48" class="ltx_figure"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2605.00737v1/predictor_bfcl_bfcl_barplot_pred2_vs_pred3_accuracy.svg" id="A6.F48.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" width="274" height="138"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 48: </span>
<span id="A6.F48.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">The LUE can predict the <span id="A6.F48.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">True Utility</span> more accurately across most models, especially for small and weaker models.</span>.
</figcaption>
</figure>
